{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\ntests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py::test_a_write_pushing_to_the_origin_leaves_no_detached_upkeep fails deterministically when run after tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py (minimal pair, 2s repro) and under the wider push-suite selection recorded earlier; it passes solo. Reproduced on origin/main a1a6a151bc and re-confirmed on aeab106820 (the spawn_detached/snapshot-GC merges did NOT fix it).\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by driven experiment)\n\nCross-module monkeypatch capture via a by-value import, aggravated by lazy first import:\n\n1. tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py:22 monkeypatches `lock.canonical_tracker` to a lambda returning ITS OWN tmp tracker.\n2. The test then calls `event_append.write_and_push(...)`; event_append.py:350 lazily imports `rebar._store.ensures` — the FIRST import of that module in the process.\n3. ensures.py:41 imports the function BY VALUE (`from rebar._store.lock import LockTimeout, canonical_tracker, write_lock`), executing while the patch is active, so `ensures.canonical_tracker` is permanently bound to the test's lambda. monkeypatch teardown restores `lock.canonical_tracker` but not the captured copy in `ensures`.\n4. Every later `run_ensures(tracker)` in the process (ensures.py:163) canonicalizes ANY tracker to the polluter's dead tmpdir: the whole init-time ensure sweep — including the `gc-config` unit's `gc.autoDetach=false` + `maintenance.autoDetach=false` pins and the .gitignore/.gitattributes/.ensure-applied writes — lands in the wrong directory while reporting `changed`.\n5. The victim test's freshly-inited tracker is therefore UNPINNED; its `git commit` (trace2: parent argv `git -C .../.tickets-tracker commit ...`) spawns `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` at git's default autoDetach, and tests/_git_upkeep.py:203 correctly fails.\n\nRuntime evidence: instrumented run_ensures printed `raw=<victim tracker> canonical=<.../test_event_and_batch_append_ke0/.tickets-tracker> realpath_fn=<function test_event_and_batch_append_keep_the_default_push_contract.<locals>.<lambda>>`; the victim tracker post-init had no pins/no .ensure-applied while all units reported ok/changed. The fixture origin itself was correctly pinned throughout — the ticket's original \"origin past a gc threshold / trace scope\" hypothesis is rejected.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the CLASS (import-time capture), not the one run: make `ensures.py` late-bind through the module object — `from rebar._store import lock as _lock` and call `_lock.canonical_tracker` / `_lock.write_lock` / `_lock.LockTimeout` at use time — exactly the style event_append.py, sync.py, push.py already use (ensures.py is the ONLY by-value importer of these names in src/rebar; nothing imports them FROM ensures). Behavior-preserving in production; removes the capture hazard for any patch-active first import. No change to the polluter test's contract (its monkeypatch is correctly scoped and now correctly confined).\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_store/ensures.py (import + 6 call sites)\n- tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py (new regression test)\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN regression test pinning the mechanism: pop `rebar._store.ensures` from sys.modules, import it while `lock.canonical_tracker` is monkeypatched to a decoy path, exit the patch, then assert `applied_ids(real_tracker)` reads the REAL tracker's `.ensure-applied` (old code: reads the decoy → fails RED). Test restores a clean ensures import in a finally so it cannot itself pollute. Plus: the minimal pair (test_push_callers_best_effort.py + the inline upkeep test) and the full recorded 14-suite selection pass deterministically; the upkeep oracle keeps its teeth (tests/_git_upkeep.py assertion unchanged — a genuinely unpinned remote still fails).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Root cause of the ordering-dependent detached upkeep is confirmed with a driven experiment (cited path:line evidence on the ticket).\n- [x] The recorded reproduction selection and the minimal pair pass deterministically after the fix.\n- [x] A regression test fails RED on the pre-fix import-capture mechanism and passes GREEN after.\n- [x] test_a_write_pushing_to_the_origin_leaves_no_detached_upkeep still fails RED when a push genuinely leaves detached upkeep (the oracle keeps its teeth)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787356062792787001,"uuid":"44a3ac8c-90fc-4edc-b599-bcec4cb6067b"}